# Normalize text; force CRLF where .editorconfig demands it (end_of_line = crlf) so Linux CI
# checkouts match Windows working trees for every tool that reads .editorconfig
# (dotnet format, IDE format-on-save).
* text=auto
*.cs text eol=crlf
# The frontend uses Prettier's line endings (LF) everywhere, so `prettier --check` agrees on Windows
# checkouts (core.autocrlf) and in Linux CI (c003 design.md § Bootstrap).
src/RevolutReader.Web/** text eol=lf
# The OpenAPI document as the export check writes it (LF), so a Windows checkout and the CI drift
# step compare the same bytes (c007 design.md D9). The generated TypeScript types sit under the line above.
src/RevolutReader.Api/openapi.json text eol=lf
# Images are binary, also in the frontend: as text, their bytes would be rewritten on commit (a PNG's
# signature holds a CRLF). After the line above, so it wins.
*.png binary
